1
00:00:03,433 --> 00:00:04,533
I'm Peppa Pig.

2
00:00:05,399 --> 00:00:07,500
This is my little brother George.

3
00:00:08,166 --> 00:00:09,466
This is Mommy Pig.

4
00:00:10,433 --> 00:00:12,133
And this is Daddy Pig.

5
00:00:14,166 --> 00:00:15,766
Peppa Pig.

6
00:00:17,633 --> 00:00:19,733
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

7
00:00:20,133 --> 00:00:23,466
[narrator] Grandpa Pig is taking
Peppa and George on a boat trip.

8
00:00:24,633 --> 00:00:26,366
Polly Parrot is going, too.

9
00:00:26,433 --> 00:00:27,299
[squawks]

10
00:00:27,366 --> 00:00:31,400
Grandpa Pig.
Have you got your mobile phone?

11
00:00:31,466 --> 00:00:33,500
Yes, Granny Pig.

12
00:00:33,566 --> 00:00:35,600
Don't drop it in the water.

13
00:00:35,666 --> 00:00:37,566
No, Granny Pig.

14
00:00:37,633 --> 00:00:39,066
Is it switched on?

15
00:00:39,133 --> 00:00:41,000
Yes, Granny Pig.

16
00:00:41,066 --> 00:00:42,100
Bye.

17
00:00:42,166 --> 00:00:43,266
-Bye-bye.
-Bye-bye.

18
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:46,066
[narrator] Here is Granddad Dog.

19
00:00:46,533 --> 00:00:48,000
Ahoy there.

20
00:00:48,066 --> 00:00:50,099
Ruff. Ahoy there.

21
00:00:50,166 --> 00:00:52,099
Lovely day to go sailing.

22
00:00:52,166 --> 00:00:55,099
I would go, too,
but my boat needs a clean.

23
00:00:55,166 --> 00:00:56,066
[laughs]

24
00:00:56,133 --> 00:00:59,766
I'm don't know why you bother cleaning
that rusty boat.

25
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,400
I'm surprised it's still afloat.

26
00:01:02,466 --> 00:01:05,800
This rusty boat will still be afloat

27
00:01:06,033 --> 00:01:10,133
long after your old tin boat has sunk
to the bottom of the river.

28
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:11,666
[barking and oinking]

29
00:01:11,733 --> 00:01:14,466
[narrator] Granddad Dog
is Grandpa Pig's very best friend.

30
00:01:15,100 --> 00:01:18,166
Full steam ahead. Goodbye.

31
00:01:19,266 --> 00:01:22,333
I am the captain of this boat,

32
00:01:22,399 --> 00:01:27,333
and when the captain tells you
to do something, you must do it.

33
00:01:27,399 --> 00:01:29,133
[both] Aye, aye, captain.

34
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:30,366
Aye, aye, captain.

35
00:01:30,433 --> 00:01:31,533
[kids laughing]

36
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:34,399
[narrator] Polly Parrot copies everything
that is said.

37
00:01:34,466 --> 00:01:37,000
George, raise the flag.

38
00:01:37,066 --> 00:01:39,199
George, raise the flag.

39
00:01:39,266 --> 00:01:40,366
[laughs]

40
00:01:41,033 --> 00:01:43,333
Peppa, ring the bell.

41
00:01:43,399 --> 00:01:45,500
Peppa, ring the bell.

42
00:01:47,399 --> 00:01:51,100
Grandpa, can I be the captain? Please.

43
00:01:51,166 --> 00:01:56,233
Okay, but as captain,
you must wear this hat.

44
00:01:56,300 --> 00:02:00,466
[narrator] Now Peppa is the captain
and everyone must do what she says.

45
00:02:00,533 --> 00:02:01,600
Ding the bell.

46
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:04,199
Turn that wheel.

47
00:02:04,266 --> 00:02:06,399
Aye, aye, Captain Peppa.

48
00:02:07,033 --> 00:02:08,433
Jump up and down.

49
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:12,700
[narrator] Captain Peppa is a bit bossy.

50
00:02:12,766 --> 00:02:15,466
Perhaps I should be the captain again.

51
00:02:15,533 --> 00:02:18,100
We don't want to crash into anything.

52
00:02:18,633 --> 00:02:22,366
Steering the boat can be tricky.

53
00:02:22,433 --> 00:02:25,566
Luckily, I'm good at steering.

54
00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:26,766
[all gasp]

55
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:31,600
[narrator] Oh, dear. Grandpa Pig's boat
has crashed into a little island.

56
00:02:33,766 --> 00:02:36,233
Grandpa, we're stuck.

57
00:02:36,299 --> 00:02:39,766
I'll ring Granny Pig. She can get help.

58
00:02:41,166 --> 00:02:42,400
[squawks]

59
00:02:42,466 --> 00:02:43,666
[shouts]

60
00:02:45,200 --> 00:02:48,266
[narrator] Grandpa Pig has dropped
his phone in the water.

61
00:02:49,799 --> 00:02:51,100
[ringing]

62
00:02:51,166 --> 00:02:53,366
Granny Pig speaking. Hello?

63
00:02:54,100 --> 00:02:56,600
Hello? Hello?

64
00:02:57,233 --> 00:03:01,366
Somehow, we need to get a message
to Granny.

65
00:03:02,133 --> 00:03:03,100
Message to Granny.

66
00:03:03,633 --> 00:03:05,733
Polly can fly to Granny.

67
00:03:05,799 --> 00:03:10,799
Good idea, Peppa.
And I can teach Polly what to say.

68
00:03:11,533 --> 00:03:13,633
Grandpa Pig says--

69
00:03:13,700 --> 00:03:15,633
"Grandpa Pig says--"

70
00:03:15,700 --> 00:03:17,533
--help, help.

71
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:19,200
--"help, help."

72
00:03:19,266 --> 00:03:22,299
There you see. Easy peasy.

73
00:03:22,366 --> 00:03:25,200
Grandpa Pig says, "Easy peasy."

74
00:03:25,266 --> 00:03:27,233
You silly old bird.

75
00:03:27,299 --> 00:03:29,533
You silly old bird.

76
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:34,566
Hello, Polly. What are you doing here?

77
00:03:34,633 --> 00:03:35,633
[squawks]

78
00:03:35,700 --> 00:03:37,566
Grandpa Pig says...

79
00:03:37,633 --> 00:03:40,033
What does Grandpa Pig say?

80
00:03:40,100 --> 00:03:42,399
-"You silly old bird.
-Oh!

81
00:03:42,466 --> 00:03:43,766
Help. Help."

82
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:46,433
Goodness me. Grandpa must need help.

83
00:03:49,333 --> 00:03:51,066
Granddad Dog.

84
00:03:51,133 --> 00:03:52,799
Hello, Granny Pig.

85
00:03:53,033 --> 00:03:57,233
Grandpa Pig needs help.
Please, could you rescue him?

86
00:03:57,299 --> 00:04:00,299
Madame, I would be delighted.

87
00:04:01,766 --> 00:04:03,033
[horn blows]

88
00:04:03,100 --> 00:04:04,200
-Hooray.
-Hooray.

89
00:04:04,266 --> 00:04:07,433
Ahoy there. Do you need rescuing, captain?

90
00:04:07,500 --> 00:04:09,500
Um, maybe.

91
00:04:09,566 --> 00:04:14,033
Would you like my rusty old boat
to rescue you?

92
00:04:14,100 --> 00:04:16,766
Yes, please, Granddad Dog.

93
00:04:17,399 --> 00:04:18,399
Catch this, captain.

94
00:04:18,466 --> 00:04:20,233
Aye, aye, skipper.

95
00:04:20,300 --> 00:04:24,433
[narrator] Granddad Dog
is Grandpa Pig's very best friend.

96
00:04:25,433 --> 00:04:29,366
Granny, did Polly tell you we needed help?

97
00:04:29,433 --> 00:04:33,099
Yes. Polly is a very clever parrot.

98
00:04:33,566 --> 00:04:36,166
Say, "I'm a clever parrot."

99
00:04:36,466 --> 00:04:37,633
[barking]

100
00:04:37,700 --> 00:04:39,599
"I'm a clever parrot."

101
00:04:40,066 --> 00:04:41,033
[barking]

102
00:04:41,099 --> 00:04:42,700
[all laughing]

103
00:04:47,666 --> 00:04:50,500
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

104
00:04:50,599 --> 00:04:52,133
[phone ringing]

105
00:04:55,200 --> 00:04:57,333
Hello. Daddy Pig speaking.

106
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:59,000
[person speaking in French]

107
00:04:59,066 --> 00:05:02,066
Oh. Something's wrong with the phone.

108
00:05:03,566 --> 00:05:06,599
You see? The phone's talking nonsense.

109
00:05:06,666 --> 00:05:07,533
Hello?

110
00:05:07,599 --> 00:05:09,166
[both speaking in French]

111
00:05:12,500 --> 00:05:15,800
[in English] That was Monsieur Donkey.
He was speaking French.

112
00:05:16,033 --> 00:05:17,733
Ha! I thought as much.

113
00:05:18,366 --> 00:05:21,733
Mommy, what did Monsieur Donkey say?

114
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:25,066
He asked if little Delphine Donkey
could visit us.

115
00:05:25,133 --> 00:05:26,233
Oh, goody.

116
00:05:26,300 --> 00:05:29,366
[narrator] Delphine Donkey
is Peppa's very special friend

117
00:05:29,433 --> 00:05:30,300
from France.

118
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:34,266
Delphine's coming
to practice talking English with us.

119
00:05:34,333 --> 00:05:35,300
-Hooray.
-Hooray.

120
00:05:35,366 --> 00:05:39,000
We'd better hurry, Delphine's train
is arriving any minute.

121
00:05:41,533 --> 00:05:44,099
Last stop. All change.

122
00:05:44,166 --> 00:05:46,800
[Peppa] That's Delphine's train.

123
00:05:48,300 --> 00:05:49,400
Delphine.

124
00:05:49,466 --> 00:05:50,533
[speaks in French]

125
00:05:50,599 --> 00:05:53,333
[narrator] Bonjour means hello in French.

126
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:55,266
[both speak in French then laugh]

127
00:05:57,700 --> 00:05:59,400
Bonjour, Mr. Donkey.

128
00:06:00,066 --> 00:06:03,766
My goodness.
Is that huge case for Delphine?

129
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:07,533
Yes. Delphine has brought
a few little things for her visit,

130
00:06:07,599 --> 00:06:13,366
things you do not have over here,
cheese, bread, tomatoes, water.

131
00:06:14,566 --> 00:06:15,766
Au revoir, Delphine.

132
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:18,400
I will pick you up tomorrow night.

133
00:06:21,500 --> 00:06:23,799
Where shall I put Delphine's luggage?

134
00:06:24,033 --> 00:06:27,333
In my room. At the very top of the house.

135
00:06:27,400 --> 00:06:28,466
Oh.

136
00:06:31,266 --> 00:06:34,033
And this luggage
is for one night's stay?

137
00:06:34,099 --> 00:06:39,099
Oh, yes. That is why
I only pack a little bag.

138
00:06:39,166 --> 00:06:40,400
[grunts]

139
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:43,633
Now, Delphine is here to practice
talking English,

140
00:06:43,700 --> 00:06:45,599
so we must all help her.

141
00:06:45,666 --> 00:06:47,133
Yes, Mommy.

142
00:06:48,066 --> 00:06:52,799
First, I must say sorry,
I do not speak English very well.

143
00:06:53,033 --> 00:06:55,233
You don't speak too badly.

144
00:06:55,299 --> 00:06:57,466
You are very kind, Monsieur Pig.

145
00:06:57,533 --> 00:07:01,633
But may I ask you a question
about talking English?

146
00:07:01,700 --> 00:07:05,200
Of course. I'm an expert at talking.

147
00:07:05,266 --> 00:07:06,233
Ask away.

148
00:07:06,299 --> 00:07:12,566
Are English split-infinitives a form
of irregular verb or past-pronoun?

149
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,166
Uh...

150
00:07:14,233 --> 00:07:18,000
Actually, it's quite late.
Shall we set up Delphine's bed?

151
00:07:18,066 --> 00:07:21,799
Mommy, Mommy,
can Delphine sleep in my bed,

152
00:07:22,033 --> 00:07:24,200
with a pillow at each end?

153
00:07:24,266 --> 00:07:25,500
Good idea, Peppa.

154
00:07:25,566 --> 00:07:29,233
[narrator] Peppa and Delphine are sleeping
at each end of the same bed.

155
00:07:29,299 --> 00:07:31,000
[giggling]

156
00:07:31,066 --> 00:07:33,166
Now children, try to go to sleep.

157
00:07:33,700 --> 00:07:35,633
You've got a busy day tomorrow.

158
00:07:35,700 --> 00:07:38,033
Delphine is visiting your playgroup.

159
00:07:38,299 --> 00:07:39,266
Wow.

160
00:07:39,333 --> 00:07:40,433
[speaks in French]

161
00:07:40,500 --> 00:07:43,400
[narrator]
Dormez bien is French for sleep well.

162
00:07:44,366 --> 00:07:46,233
I'm not sleepy at all.

163
00:07:47,133 --> 00:07:50,366
Let's sing a little song
to make us sleepy.

164
00:07:50,433 --> 00:07:51,299
Yes.

165
00:07:52,599 --> 00:07:54,466
[singing in French]

166
00:08:02,166 --> 00:08:06,266
[narrator] Delphine's pretty French song
has sent everyone to sleep.

167
00:08:11,133 --> 00:08:14,166
Delphine has come
to visit Peppa's playgroup.

168
00:08:15,766 --> 00:08:21,099
Madame Gazelle, this is my French friend,
Delphine Donkey.

169
00:08:21,366 --> 00:08:22,633
[speaks in French]

170
00:08:22,700 --> 00:08:25,000
Ah! Bonjour, Delphine.

171
00:08:25,066 --> 00:08:29,366
Delphine sang a pretty French song
last night.

172
00:08:29,433 --> 00:08:32,000
Can we teach her an English song?

173
00:08:32,466 --> 00:08:35,133
How about the "Bing Bong" song?

174
00:08:35,199 --> 00:08:40,299
Yes, sing me this "Bing Bong" song.
It would be good for my English.

175
00:08:40,766 --> 00:08:41,633
Okay.

176
00:08:42,299 --> 00:08:43,666
Ooh!

177
00:08:44,566 --> 00:08:47,766
We're playing a tune
And we're singing a song

178
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:50,566
With a bing and bong and a bing

179
00:08:52,033 --> 00:08:55,433
Bong bing boo, bing bong bing

180
00:08:55,500 --> 00:08:59,033
Bing bong bingly bungly boo

181
00:08:59,100 --> 00:09:02,533
Bong bing boo, bing bong bing

182
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:06,066
Bing bong bingly bungly boo

183
00:09:06,133 --> 00:09:10,100
Good. I have learnt lots
of new English words.

184
00:09:10,533 --> 00:09:14,666
Bing, bong, bingly, bungly, boo.

185
00:09:14,733 --> 00:09:16,666
[all laughing]

186
00:09:19,466 --> 00:09:21,733
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

187
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:24,133
[narrator]
Mommy Pig is dressed as a fireman.

188
00:09:24,600 --> 00:09:27,366
Mommy, why are you dressed like that?

189
00:09:28,133 --> 00:09:31,466
I'm going
to the Mommies Fire Engine practice.

190
00:09:31,533 --> 00:09:33,133
Ooh!

191
00:09:33,199 --> 00:09:36,666
It's just a good excuse
for a cup of tea and a chat.

192
00:09:36,733 --> 00:09:39,600
Well, what are you doing today,
Daddy Pig?

193
00:09:39,666 --> 00:09:44,266
I've got a very important meeting
with the Daddies Football Team.

194
00:09:44,333 --> 00:09:48,366
That's just a lot of grown-up boys
kicking a football around.

195
00:09:48,433 --> 00:09:50,133
We're having a barbeque as well.

196
00:09:50,199 --> 00:09:51,500
[door bell rings]

197
00:09:51,566 --> 00:09:56,699
[narrator] Here are Mr. Bull, Mr. Rabbit,
Mr. Pony, and Mr. Zebra.

198
00:09:57,800 --> 00:10:00,566
Is Daddy Pig coming out to play?

199
00:10:01,333 --> 00:10:02,500
Come on.

200
00:10:04,800 --> 00:10:08,199
Mommy, can we see the fire engine?

201
00:10:08,266 --> 00:10:10,199
-Yes.
-Oh, goody.

202
00:10:14,533 --> 00:10:17,033
[narrator]
This is Miss Rabbit's Fire Station.

203
00:10:18,199 --> 00:10:20,300
Hello, Peppa and George.

204
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:22,400
Come and see the fire engine.

205
00:10:23,333 --> 00:10:25,266
-Wow!
-Fire engine.

206
00:10:25,333 --> 00:10:28,033
There's a ladder for climbing.

207
00:10:28,100 --> 00:10:31,166
A hose for squirting water.

208
00:10:31,233 --> 00:10:33,266
And a big bell, to ring.

209
00:10:34,199 --> 00:10:36,133
Ding, dong, ding, dong.

210
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:40,766
Now, let's go up the tower
and look for fires.

211
00:10:41,666 --> 00:10:45,533
-Hello, everyone.
-Hello, Peppa. Hello, George.

212
00:10:46,266 --> 00:10:49,699
Who's for a nice cup of tea and a chat?

213
00:10:49,766 --> 00:10:51,333
That sounds nice.

214
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:53,733
Ooh! A telephone.

215
00:10:53,800 --> 00:10:57,199
Peppa, that is the fire phone.

216
00:10:57,266 --> 00:11:00,000
It's only to be used when there's a fire.

217
00:11:00,066 --> 00:11:00,766
[ringing]

218
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:03,466
Aah! Fire. Fire.

219
00:11:04,166 --> 00:11:07,699
Fire station, where's the fire?
Where's the fire?

220
00:11:07,766 --> 00:11:10,233
[Daddy Pig]
Can I speak to Mommy Pig, please?

221
00:11:10,300 --> 00:11:12,266
Oh, it's Daddy Pig.

222
00:11:12,333 --> 00:11:15,633
Daddy Pig, you're not supposed
to ring on this phone.

223
00:11:15,699 --> 00:11:17,800
It's only for emergencies.

224
00:11:18,033 --> 00:11:23,266
This is an emergency. I can't find
the tomato ketchup anywhere.

225
00:11:23,333 --> 00:11:26,066
Daddy Pig, shall I light the barbeque now?

226
00:11:26,133 --> 00:11:27,666
Yes, please, Mr. Rabbit.

227
00:11:28,300 --> 00:11:30,266
Do be careful with the barbeque,
Daddy Pig.

228
00:11:30,333 --> 00:11:35,699
Trust me, Mommy Pig, we daddies know
all about barbeques. Bye.

229
00:11:37,199 --> 00:11:39,300
Maybe it needs more charcoal?

230
00:11:39,366 --> 00:11:41,133
Give it a bit of a blow.

231
00:11:41,199 --> 00:11:44,033
Put a few more firelighters on.

232
00:11:45,300 --> 00:11:47,800
Now, we just have to wait for a fire.

233
00:11:48,033 --> 00:11:50,233
How long do we have to wait?

234
00:11:50,300 --> 00:11:54,633
Oh, it could be a long time.
I've been waiting ages.

235
00:11:54,699 --> 00:11:57,566
How many fires
have you actually put out, Miss Rabbit?

236
00:11:58,199 --> 00:12:01,366
Uh, none. Not one fire.

237
00:12:01,433 --> 00:12:03,133
But you've got to be ready.

238
00:12:03,199 --> 00:12:04,766
[ringing]

239
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:06,266
It's the fire phone.

240
00:12:06,333 --> 00:12:08,100
Oh, can you answer it Peppa?

241
00:12:08,166 --> 00:12:11,100
-It'll probably be your daddy again.
-Okay.

242
00:12:12,166 --> 00:12:14,466
Hello. Fire Station.

243
00:12:14,533 --> 00:12:17,699
-Hello, Peppa.
-Oh, Daddy. It is you.

244
00:12:17,766 --> 00:12:23,000
You're very naughty.
This phone is for fires only.

245
00:12:23,066 --> 00:12:26,266
Can you put Miss Rabbit on?
There's a good girl.

246
00:12:26,333 --> 00:12:28,733
Daddy wants to speak to you.

247
00:12:28,800 --> 00:12:33,233
Hello, Daddy Pig, this phone
is only to be used when there's a--

248
00:12:33,300 --> 00:12:34,166
Fire.

249
00:12:34,233 --> 00:12:35,400
[all] Fire. Fire. Fire.

250
00:12:35,466 --> 00:12:38,766
[narrator] Oh, dear. Daddy Pig's barbeque
is on fire.

251
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:41,199
Fire. Fire.

252
00:12:41,266 --> 00:12:42,533
Mommies to the rescue.

253
00:12:42,599 --> 00:12:44,466
Whee!

254
00:12:46,733 --> 00:12:48,033
Hold tight.

255
00:12:55,133 --> 00:12:59,366
Fire. Fire. Ding dong. Ding dong.

256
00:12:59,433 --> 00:13:01,166
[laughing]

257
00:13:02,333 --> 00:13:04,433
It's Miss Rabbit's fire engine.

258
00:13:04,500 --> 00:13:05,666
Hooray.

259
00:13:05,733 --> 00:13:07,599
Stand back, Daddies.

260
00:13:08,433 --> 00:13:11,099
Mommy Dog? Turn on the water.

261
00:13:11,166 --> 00:13:12,699
Aye, aye, Mommy Pig.

262
00:13:15,466 --> 00:13:17,000
[narrator] The fire is out.

263
00:13:17,066 --> 00:13:18,266
Hooray!

264
00:13:18,333 --> 00:13:21,800
-Thank you for saving us, Miss Rabbit.
-No problem.

265
00:13:22,033 --> 00:13:24,433
It's all part of the service.

266
00:13:24,500 --> 00:13:27,033
The Mummies Fire Engine Service.

267
00:13:27,500 --> 00:13:32,033
And now that Miss Rabbit
has kindly flooded our garden,

268
00:13:32,099 --> 00:13:35,733
we can all jump up and down
in muddy puddles.

269
00:13:35,800 --> 00:13:36,800
Yes!

270
00:13:37,699 --> 00:13:40,300
I love fire engines.

271
00:13:40,366 --> 00:13:44,166
Especially when they make muddy puddles.

272
00:13:44,233 --> 00:13:46,266
[all laughing]

273
00:13:49,500 --> 00:13:52,333
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

274
00:13:54,033 --> 00:13:56,166
[narrator]
It is bedtime for Peppa and George.

275
00:13:56,233 --> 00:13:58,233
Good night, my little piggies.

276
00:13:59,066 --> 00:14:01,766
[narrator] Granny and Grandpa Pig
have come for dinner.

277
00:14:03,566 --> 00:14:04,533
-Hello.
-Hello.

278
00:14:04,599 --> 00:14:06,000
Hello.

279
00:14:06,066 --> 00:14:07,599
Where are Peppa and George?

280
00:14:07,666 --> 00:14:08,599
They're asleep.

281
00:14:08,666 --> 00:14:12,166
Oh, but I so wanted to see them.
Can I take a peek?

282
00:14:12,233 --> 00:14:15,199
Okay, Granny Pig, but be very quiet.

283
00:14:15,266 --> 00:14:18,733
[floor creaking]

284
00:14:20,033 --> 00:14:22,199
-Granny Pig.
-Granny Pig.

285
00:14:22,266 --> 00:14:25,666
Hello, my little darlings.
You should be asleep.

286
00:14:25,733 --> 00:14:27,666
Tell us a story.

287
00:14:27,733 --> 00:14:32,400
Okay, but only if you promise
to go straight back to sleep.

288
00:14:32,466 --> 00:14:35,400
We'll go to sleep after the story.

289
00:14:35,466 --> 00:14:38,533
All right. Once upon a time there was--

290
00:14:38,599 --> 00:14:41,166
A little boy called Pedro Pony,

291
00:14:41,233 --> 00:14:44,199
he found a magic bean.

292
00:14:44,266 --> 00:14:45,300
[Granny Pig] Oh, yes.

293
00:14:45,766 --> 00:14:49,266
Now, Pedro planted that bean and it grew

294
00:14:49,333 --> 00:14:53,000
into an enormous beanstalk
that went high into the sky.

295
00:14:53,066 --> 00:14:54,366
That's right.

296
00:14:54,433 --> 00:14:58,133
Pedro climbed to the top
of that beanstalk and found--

297
00:14:58,199 --> 00:15:00,566
A horrible big giant.

298
00:15:00,633 --> 00:15:04,433
But I don't want that. I want a princess.

299
00:15:04,500 --> 00:15:08,733
Oh, yes, there he found
a beautiful Princess Peppa,

300
00:15:09,699 --> 00:15:12,266
and Sir George, the brave knight.

301
00:15:13,166 --> 00:15:17,566
[Peppa] And a cook who makes
the most delicious food ever.

302
00:15:17,633 --> 00:15:20,000
[laughing]

303
00:15:20,066 --> 00:15:23,133
[narrator] Mommy Pig, Daddy Pig
and Grandpa Pig are waiting to eat.

304
00:15:23,199 --> 00:15:26,066
I'll go and see what's keeping Granny Pig.

305
00:15:26,733 --> 00:15:28,599
What's next in the story?

306
00:15:28,666 --> 00:15:32,699
Naughty Granny Pig.
You woke the little ones.

307
00:15:32,766 --> 00:15:37,500
We promised to sleep
when the story ends, Grandpa.

308
00:15:37,566 --> 00:15:41,000
I'm good at ending stories, Granny Pig.

309
00:15:41,066 --> 00:15:44,133
You go down stairs, I won't be long.

310
00:15:44,566 --> 00:15:47,366
There's a boy, a beanstalk,

311
00:15:47,433 --> 00:15:50,099
a beautiful princess,

312
00:15:50,166 --> 00:15:51,766
a brave knight

313
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:54,666
and a cook
who makes a lovely dinner.

314
00:15:54,733 --> 00:16:01,166
Well, after they ate the lovely dinner,
everyone fell asleep. The end.

315
00:16:01,233 --> 00:16:04,533
Then they all woke up
and along came a wizard.

316
00:16:04,599 --> 00:16:05,800
A wizard?

317
00:16:06,033 --> 00:16:11,033
[Peppa] Yes. A wizard. Who is going
to do a big magic show.

318
00:16:11,666 --> 00:16:15,466
-But--
-Then, along came a scary dragon.

319
00:16:15,533 --> 00:16:17,366
[laughs then roars]

320
00:16:18,033 --> 00:16:22,133
[narrator] Granny Pig, Mommy Pig and
Daddy Pig are still waiting to eat dinner.

321
00:16:22,199 --> 00:16:25,166
That bedtime story
doesn't seem to be working.

322
00:16:25,233 --> 00:16:28,333
I'm the expert at telling bedtime stories.

323
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:31,133
I'll have them asleep in no time.

324
00:16:32,166 --> 00:16:33,599
A scary dragon.

325
00:16:34,466 --> 00:16:36,466
Peppa. George. Back to bed.

326
00:16:37,433 --> 00:16:41,599
But Grandpa hasn't finished
the story yet, Daddy.

327
00:16:41,666 --> 00:16:46,033
I'll finish the story.
I'll be down in a minute.

328
00:16:46,766 --> 00:16:50,599
Okay, there's a boy,
a beanstalk, a castle,

329
00:16:50,666 --> 00:16:52,699
a beautiful princess,

330
00:16:52,766 --> 00:16:54,699
a brave knight, a cook,

331
00:16:54,766 --> 00:16:57,766
a wizard and a scary dragon.

332
00:16:58,433 --> 00:17:01,133
And a very hungry King.

333
00:17:01,766 --> 00:17:06,099
So they all had a big dinner
and lived happily ever after.

334
00:17:06,566 --> 00:17:07,800
The end.

335
00:17:08,033 --> 00:17:10,399
Then they had a party.

336
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:14,200
And all their friends came.

337
00:17:14,266 --> 00:17:16,266
[all laughing]

338
00:17:22,433 --> 00:17:25,000
Right. I think I'd better sort this out.

339
00:17:25,500 --> 00:17:27,166
[laughing]

340
00:17:27,233 --> 00:17:30,000
-Daddy Pig.
-They're almost asleep.

341
00:17:31,466 --> 00:17:34,399
Thank you. I'll take over now.

342
00:17:34,466 --> 00:17:37,100
You have to finish the story, Mommy.

343
00:17:37,166 --> 00:17:39,533
All right quickly now,
tell me what's happened?

344
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:44,566
Once upon a time, in olden days,
a long time ago...

345
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:48,600
Mommy Pig's been up there for a long time.

346
00:17:50,200 --> 00:17:51,800
I can hear snoring.

347
00:17:52,033 --> 00:17:55,700
At last. Peppa and George are asleep.

348
00:17:56,333 --> 00:18:02,033
...and they all lived happily ever after.
The end.

349
00:18:02,100 --> 00:18:03,733
Peppa. George.

350
00:18:03,800 --> 00:18:06,466
Shush! Mommy is asleep.

351
00:18:06,533 --> 00:18:07,633
[laughs]

352
00:18:07,700 --> 00:18:12,200
It looks like Princess Peppa
is the best at telling bedtime stories.

353
00:18:12,266 --> 00:18:14,600
That's right, I am.

354
00:18:15,100 --> 00:18:16,700
[all laughing]

